<title>SWITZERLAND: SWISS JUNE SHORT-TIME WORK FALLS 23 PCT FROM MAY.</title>
<headline>SWISS JUNE SHORT-TIME WORK FALLS 23 PCT FROM MAY.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people on short-time work in Switzerland in June fell 23.2 percent, or by 1,288, to 4,260 from May, the Swiss Federal Office for Trade, Industry and Labour said.</p>
<p>The number of companies affected dropped by 103, or 14.2 percent, to 624.</p>
<p>Lost working hours fell by 55,946, or 17.0 percent, to 273,156.</p>
<p>In June 1996, 716,430 hours had been lost among 15,136 people and 1,045 companies.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
